@startuml
!theme plain
title Mandatory host verification before user authentication (TASK-260715-2ny6z4)

participant Core
participant "SSHTransport adapter" as Adapter
participant "SSH engine / server" as Engine
participant "SSHHostKeyPolicy" as Policy
participant "SSHCredentialProvider" as Credentials

Core -> Adapter: connect(configuration)
Adapter -> Engine: TCP connect + initial KEX
Engine --> Adapter: algorithm + raw SSH host-key bytes
Adapter -> Adapter: SHA256 fingerprint from exact bytes
Adapter -> Policy: evaluate(host, endpoint, algorithm, bytes, fingerprint, lane)

alt explicit first-use record or approved match
  Policy --> Adapter: acceptFirstUse / acceptMatch
  Adapter -> Credentials: credential(reference)
  Credentials --> Adapter: public-key signer
  Adapter -> Engine: user authentication
  Engine --> Adapter: success / typed rejection
  Adapter --> Core: authenticated session or typed auth error
else unknown, changed, algorithm, or policy reject
  Policy --> Adapter: typed rejection
  Adapter -> Engine: close before user auth
  Adapter --> Core: typed host-key error
end

note over Adapter,Credentials
  E-HOSTAUTH asserts Credentials and the server user-auth
  callback are untouched on every host-policy rejection.
end note

note over Policy
  Raw key bytes and fingerprint never enter default
  logs, metrics, public errors, or telemetry.
end note
@enduml

